# std/rgrep: recursive grep. tree-map does the recursion (one job per directory,
# a sparse result tree of the same shape: only matching files appear, each
# holding its matches as `linenum:line` lines); ./level is the grep of ONE
# directory's files. `--pattern` is bound by the caller and forwarded by
# tree-map to ./level, so a child's cache key is (subtree, pattern).
#
# Flattening to classic `path:linenum:line` output is the caller's presentation
# choice (llm-step renders it at the transcript boundary).
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/tree-map --run:@=level
